# Settings of the Kassa server on this machine. The server reads them as environment variables
# (node --env-file=...). This file holds the database password: it lives outside the repository
# (C:\kassa\config\kassa.env on Windows), only administrators and the service accounts may read it,
# and it is never committed.
#
# deploy/setup-database.mjs writes it for you, with a password of its own. Edit by hand only to
# change a setting.

NODE_ENV=production
HOST=127.0.0.1
# The port the server listens on, on this machine only. Every installation on a machine has a port of its own.
PORT=3000
DATABASE_URL=postgres://kassa:CHANGE-ME@127.0.0.1:5432/kassa

# The name of this installation, when it is not the only one on the machine (the cash desk of another company):
# one short lower-case word, like express. The scripts of deploy/windows name its service (KassaApp-express) and its
# tasks (Kassa backup (express)) by it; the first installation has no name and keeps KassaApp and Kassa backup.
# setup.ps1 -Instance writes this line, with a port, a role and a database of its own: do not change it afterwards.
# INSTANCE=

# The cash desks of the company, in their order, each with the money it keeps: id:CURRENCY or id:CURRENCY+CURRENCY
# (RUB, USD), separated by commas. Without this line: moscow:RUB+USD,andijan:USD. The first one is the main desk.
# moscow, andijan and tashkent get their names by themselves; any other city is written with its name,
# fergana=Фергана:USD. Set it before the first entry: a desk that has entries is never renamed here or taken out, nor
# is a currency it has entries in taken from it (the server does not start then). Three desks that all keep dollars only:
# KASSAS=moscow:USD,andijan:USD,tashkent:USD

# The reverse proxy (Caddy) runs on this machine and tells the server the real address of each
# client in X-Forwarded-For. Without this line every client looks like 127.0.0.1, and a stranger's
# wrong passwords would lock every login out, the owner's too.
TRUST_PROXY=127.0.0.1

# Days a session lives without use (default 90).
# SESSION_DAYS=90

# Copies of the database (deploy/backup.mjs, deploy/windows/backup.ps1). Write the values without quotes.
# Where the copies go, a full path: a second disk is the point, a copy on the disk that fails is no help.
# Without this line backup.ps1 uses C:\kassa\backups.
# BACKUP_DIR=D:\kassa-copies
# How many copies to keep (default 14); older ones are deleted after each new copy.
# BACKUP_KEEP=14
# The folder with pg_dump and pg_restore, if they are not found by themselves.
# PG_BIN=C:\Program Files\PostgreSQL\16\bin

# The token of the Telegram bot of the Mini App (from @BotFather). Unset: signing in inside Telegram is off.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# The Telegram group that is told of the entries (see docs/deploy-windows.md, 3.3): its number, which starts with a minus
# (find it with: .\deploy\windows\kassa.ps1 telegram-chats). Needs the token above. Unset: no messages.
# TELEGRAM_GROUP_CHAT_ID=-1001234567890
# The topics of that group, if it has topics: one for the incomes, one for the expenses (their numbers are shown by
# telegram-chats after a command was written in each topic). A kind without a topic goes to the main topic.
# TELEGRAM_THREAD_INCOME=3
# TELEGRAM_THREAD_EXPENSE=5
# The topic of one cash desk, for all its messages (incomes, expenses, corrections, counts): TELEGRAM_THREAD_ and the id
# of the desk in capitals. Without one, the main desk (the first of KASSAS) uses the two topics above and any other desk
# the main topic.
# TELEGRAM_THREAD_ANDIJAN=7
# TELEGRAM_THREAD_TASHKENT=9

# The journal copied to a Google spreadsheet (see docs/deploy-windows.md, 3.5): the id from the address of the
# spreadsheet, the JSON key of the service account it is shared with, the first day to copy. Unset: nothing is copied.
# GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_KEY_FILE=C:\kassa\config\google-key.json
# GOOGLE_SHEET_FROM=2026-10-14
# GOOGLE_SHEET_TAB=Журнал

# Writing the payments of clients into the 1C base of the company as cash receipts. off (the default), preview (looks,
# writes nothing) or live. Take the first live steps in docs/deploy-windows.md, section 3.4: a copy of the base first.
# (A settings file written before these were named ONEC_* has them as COSMO_1C_MODE, COSMO_ODATA_URL, COSMO_ODATA_USER,
# COSMO_ODATA_PASSWORD, COSMO_1C_ORGANIZATION_KEY, COSMO_1C_KASSA_KEY, COSMO_1C_CURRENCY_KEY, COSMO_1C_CLIENTS and
# COSMO_1C_SEND: those names are still read, and a setting under its ONEC_ name wins.)
# ONEC_MODE=preview
# The address of the OData service of the base (with or without /odata/standard.odata), and the login it is read and written with.
# ONEC_ODATA_URL=
# ONEC_ODATA_USER=
# ONEC_ODATA_PASSWORD=
# The organization, the cash desk and the currency of the receipts, by their keys in the base (kassa.ps1 onec-check names them).
# ONEC_ORGANIZATION_KEY=
# ONEC_KASSA_KEY=
# ONEC_CURRENCY_KEY=
# The cash desks whose payments are written (their ids from KASSAS, comma separated); without this line the main desk only.
# A desk that has a cash desk of its own in the base names its key in ONEC_KASSA_KEY_ and its id in capitals (a key
# named after a desk that is not in KASSAS or is not written keeps the server from starting).
# ONEC_KASSAS=moscow,tashkent
# ONEC_KASSA_KEY_TASHKENT=
# Only these clients are written (codes, comma separated): for the first live receipt.
# ONEC_CLIENTS=
# When a payment goes to 1C: night (the default: at 03:00 Moscow time, when the day of the cash desk is over) or now.
# ONEC_SEND=night
